# Production deployment

- Deploy to `root@ssh.neko.shirkneko.top` (Armbian, `linux-aarch64`) with key `~/.ssh/id_ed25519`.
- Public entry: `https://themes.neko.shirkneko.top:8443/` → Lucky TLS → Caddy `127.0.0.1:8080` → app `127.0.0.1:8090`.
- Never store the SSH passphrase, tokens, or `store.env` contents in the repo. Ask the user to unlock the key, or use a session-only `SUKISU_SSH_PASS` with an askpass helper.
- Windows OpenSSH `ControlMaster`/`ControlPath` is broken on this host. Use one SSH invocation per operation or stream a tar/script over stdin.
- Build: `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/build-aarch64.ps1`
  - Output: `target/aarch64-unknown-linux-musl/release/sukisu-theme-web`
- Service: `sukisu-theme-web.service`; binary `/opt/sukisu-theme-web/sukisu-theme-web-rs`; listens on `127.0.0.1:8090`.
- `THEME_STATIC_DIR` is not set. All HTML/CSS/JS/locales/logo are embedded in the binary; rebuild and replace the binary for every static change.
- Storage locations: `/etc/sukisu-theme-web/sources.json` (`THEME_SOURCES_FILE`), mode 0600. Types: local/NAS mount and OpenList/AList. Sources can be read-only import or writable overflow locations with per-location quota/priority. Primary storage is always first; existing themes stay at their original location (`storageId`/`_loc` key prefix). Back up this file with the config.
- AList must already have the cloud drive/share mounted; never implement share-link scraping or rate-limit bypass.
- Caddy: `/etc/caddy/Caddyfile`. Keep the `@ui_assets path /i18n.js /locales/*` → `reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8090` route before the token gate or language assets return 401. Add any new root-level public asset to `@ui_assets`; pages use `/admin/logo.svg` and `/account/logo.svg`.
- Backups: `/root/sukisu-deploy-backup/<timestamp>` and `/root/caddy-deploy-backup/Caddyfile.<timestamp>`.
- Read `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` for commands, verification, rollback, and troubleshooting.
